{
  "_comment": [
    "Bucket spec for /stats/home treatmentSubcategories.",
    "",
    "Each bucket can match terms three ways (apply in order; OR-combined within a bucket):",
    "  parentSubtreeUris — ontology parent URIs; expanded via OntologyService.getChildren",
    "                      (CHEBI must be loaded for these to populate; otherwise 0).",
    "  uriPrefixes       — exact valueUri prefix match (startsWith).",
    "  uriExactMatches   — full-URI equality match.",
    "",
    "Bucket order is first-match-wins: a term that's both a drug AND a hormone lands",
    "in the bucket listed first.",
    "",
    "Optional fields:",
    "  group       — coarse UI category, used by the frontend to cluster bars together",
    "                visually. Recommended values: control, pharmacology, biological,",
    "                unclassified. Lets the UI separate 'control-like' bars (control +",
    "                vehicle) from pharmacology of interest without baking that into",
    "                the order of the bar chart.",
    "  subBuckets  — nested partition. When a term matches this bucket, it is ALSO",
    "                matched against the sub-buckets (first-match-wins). Each matched",
    "                term is attributed to exactly one sub-bucket — or to an implicit",
    "                <key>_other sub-bucket if none match. Parent count = Σ child count.",
    "                Sub-buckets carry the same fields as top-level buckets; can nest",
    "                further if needed.",
    "",
    "Two catchalls are emitted automatically:",
    "  other_chemical   — CHEBI URIs not in any explicit bucket. group=unclassified.",
    "  other            — non-CHEBI URIs not in any explicit bucket. group=unclassified.",
    "",
    "Top 15 terms by EE-mention count are reported on every bucket as topTerms[],",
    "including the catchalls — that's the iterative-bucketing loop: scan the head of",
    "other_chemical / other, move whatever's pharmacologically meaningful into a more",
    "specific bucket here, redeploy.",
    "",
    "To override: drop a treatment-buckets.json into ${gemma.appdata.home}/HomeStats/.",
    "If present it replaces this classpath default. Otherwise this file ships."
  ],
  "buckets": [
    {
      "_comment": "Vehicles / solvent controls. Listed FIRST so e.g. DMSO matches `vehicle` before falling through into the broader CHEBI:23888 'drug' subtree under `approved_drug`. group=control so the UI can cluster it with the explicit control bucket (both are accurate annotations but not pharmacology of interest).",
      "key": "vehicle",
      "label": "Vehicles / solvents",
      "group": "control",
      "uriExactMatches": [
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_28262",
        "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_16236",
